Dependency distribution boundary
--------------------------------
Mediabunny is MPL-2.0. Vela pins its fork (https://github.com/alchemyyy/mediabunny,
commit e9303e8dbf1e77140328a417ac07306defc42cf6) as the mediabunny package; the player
payload ships its source as sources/mediabunny.tar.gz.
Decoder packages are separately licensed: FFmpeg/libdcadec based packages are
LGPL-2.1-or-later. Their manifests, licence texts and exact corresponding source
archives must accompany the independently loaded modules when distributed.
Do not infer those packages are MIT from the engine licence. Runtime package
installation must retain source/replacement information and verified version
identities. Production runtime payloads retain these notices and corresponding
sources alongside their independently loaded decoder packages.
The unlicensed Jellyfin host plugin is not included or copied.

Subtitle distributions
----------------------
Optional JASSUB 1.8.8 assets are independently loaded. The wrapper is MIT;
libass is ISC, FriBidi LGPL-2.1-or-later, FreeType FTL, HarfBuzz MIT/NTP,
and Brotli MIT. Noto Sans fallback fonts use SIL OFL 1.1. The verified subtitle
asset distribution includes JASSUB-COPYRIGHT.txt, font licences, exact matching
source archives/build scripts and SOURCE-OFFER.txt. The pinned revisions, hashes
and source URLs are in modules/vela-player/web/engine/universal/subtitles/assets.json.

Native playback (libmpv)
------------------------
Apple platforms (tvOS, iOS and the macOS desktop host) play through AetherEngine 7.70.0
(LGPL-3.0 with an App Store exception, unmodified), its dynamic LGPL FFmpeg frameworks from
FFmpegBuild 3.15.0 (no GPL or nonfree components), LibDovi (MIT) and, for TrueHD Atmos object
rendering, LibTrueHD 3.2.0 (MIT) with the truehdd `truehd` and `oamd` crates (Apache-2.0).
DTS:X heights are decoded by FFmpeg itself. The texts and notices ship in the app's
VelaPlayerLicenses bundle (modules/vela-player/ios/Licenses); see
modules/vela-player/ios/AETHER.md for the optional components and their licensing.
Android builds libmpv with -Dgpl=false and FFmpeg without --enable-gpl (LGPLv3 because
of --enable-version3) from libmpv-android, pinned in modules/vela-player/android/libmpv/pin.sh.
The Windows host loads libmpv-2.dll at runtime. It is the LGPL build of mpv-winbuild-cmake
(mpv -Dgpl=false; FFmpeg without --enable-gpl/--enable-nonfree, LGPLv3 through
--enable-version3), pinned by SHA-256 in apps/vela-windows/build.ps1, which refuses a GPL
build. It ships with apps/vela-windows/licenses (licence texts, provenance, source offer).
The Linux desktop builds FFmpeg 8.0.1 (GPL and nonfree off), dav1d 1.5.3 (BSD-2-Clause),
libplacebo 7.387.0 and libmpv (-Dgpl=false, pinned mpv commit) with
apps/vela-desktop/linux/build-libraries.sh, keeping source archives and notices beside them.

Apple TV media framework (FFmpeg)
---------------------------------
native/apple/media/build-ffmpeg.sh builds VelaMedia.framework from FFmpeg 7.1.2
(LGPL-2.1-or-later, no GPL or nonfree components) as a separately linked, replaceable
library, and keeps the pinned source archive and licence beside it.

Web audio decoder (FFmpeg WebAssembly)
--------------------------------------
modules/vela-player/web/engine/universal/audio/ffmpeg builds an LGPL-2.1-or-later FFmpeg
WebAssembly decoder; its distribution carries the FFmpeg and bridge sources, the LGPL text
and VELA-AUDIO-SOURCE.txt (see the README in that directory).

Fonts
-----
Bundled fonts are under the SIL Open Font License 1.1 unless noted:
- apps/vela/assets/fonts: Instrument Serif (licence in
  packages/protocol/fixtures/skins/index/licences), Fredoka and Pixelify Sans (licences in
  packages/protocol/fixtures/skins/mochi/licences).
- Built-in skins under packages/protocol/fixtures/skins carry their fonts' licence texts
  in each skin's licences/ directory (Permanent Marker is Apache-2.0).

Windows host
------------
apps/vela-windows uses the Microsoft.Web.WebView2 NuGet package under its own licence.

